The Assembellion Commission, which is currently drafting legislation to change names, noted: "The final decision on the new name of the members of the Assembly will certainly be made by the members themselves."
The Welsh Self-Government Act of 2017 grants the Waltz Assembly the right to change its name.
In June, the commission published the results of a public discussion of the proposals, and the renaming of the Assembly to the Wales Parliament received widespread support.
Regarding how to call Ch, the commission proposes to call them "Members of Welsh Parliament", i.e. WMP, but the MWP option received the greatest support from the public.
