Increasingly it's more obvious that the LeBar Party doesn't allow different views and every opinion is evaluated from the standpoint of whether it's acceptable for the party's leadership.
This began shortly after Jeremy became the leader. Colleagues, with whom I used to think I had such political views, began to expect that I will turn 180 degrees and accept positions with which I would never agree, whether it is national security or the EU's single market.
Whenever I speak publicly — and it doesn't matter what I'm saying — followed by the tiara of attacks on social media calling for recall, condemning the center's policies, I'm told that I shouldn't be in the Labour Party.
