I've never hid my policies, including the last election.
No one in Nottingham East was embarrassed by my political views and disagreements with the current leadership.
For those who contributed to Friday's events, I want to say only one thing: in an environment where the country is marching to Brexit that will harm households, enterprises and public services, I don't understand the desire to spend time and energy on my loyalty to the leader of the Labour Party.
In fact, I have one more message, but it is not for the Notingham "Momentum", but for my voters, both members of the Labor Party and not: I am proud to serve you, and I promise that no threats to revvoke me and no political benefits will prevent me from acting according to what I consider to be the best interests of you all.
