What is a Global Citizen Festival and how can it affect poverty reduction?
On this Saturday, New York will host the Global Citizen Festival (Festival of Citizens of the World) - an annual event in the music world with an amazing number of stellar performers and an equally striking mission to overcome poverty all over the whole world.
During the Seventh Global Citizen Festival, tens of thousands of people will circulate on the Great Glade of the Central Park not just to enjoy the performances of Janet Jackson, Cardi and Sean Mendes, as well as to draw attention to the true purpose of the festival – the organisers are striving to overcome an extreme form of poverty by 2030.
The Global Citizen Festival, which was launched in 2012, is a sequel to the Global Poverty Project, an international public organization that hopes to eradicate poverty by increasing the number of people who will actively deal with it.
In order to receive a free ticket for an event (unless you want to pay for a VIP-ticket), visitors must complete a number of assignments or "devices", such to take part in a volunteer project, write an e-mail to the world leader, make a phone call or anything else to help draw attention to the organization's goal - to eradicate poverty.
Therefore, are there already any results, because there are only 12 years left to achieve the goal of Global Citizen organizers?
Is it really the idea of awarding a free gamous concert – a genital way to convince people to demand actions, is it just another case of so-called "cultivism" when people feel that they really change something by signing an e-petition or making a publication on Twitter?
According to Global Citizen, since 2011, they have spotted 19 million "decisions" of their adherents aimed at achieving a variety of goals.
The organization argues that these actions have prompted the world's leaders to state planned financial appropriations and programs worth more than $ 37 billion, which by 2030 will help change the lives of more than 2.25 billion people.
At the beginning of 2018, the group cited 390 financial liabilities and public statements as an example of the results of its activities, with at least 10 billion has already been collected and expended.
According to the group's estimates, the received funds have already directly affected the lives of approximately 649 million people around the world.
Among the main financial obligations can be recalled by The Power of Nutrition (Food Power), which territorially relates to the United Kingdom. As part of the project, investors and implementers undertook to “assist children to grow up” and promised to provide Rwanda $ 35 million in assistance to overcome the problem of malnutrition after receiving more than 4,700 tweets from Global Citizens.
"With the support of the United Kingdom's government, philanthropists, governments of other countries and citizens of the world, such as you, we can make the social problem of malnutrition insignificant fact of history," told The Power of Nutrition representative Tracy Ullman, speaking to the public during a live concert in London in April 2018.
The organization also stated that after 5000 "decisions, which called for improved nutrition of mothers and children, the British government has announced the allocating funds for The Power of Nutrition project aimed at improving the nutrition of 5 million mothers and children.
Responding to one circulatory question on your website "Which do you think you're going to be able to overcome the extreme level of poverty?"
Global Citizen representatives wrote: "It's a long and difficult path, so sometimes we're going to fall and will fail.
However, as well as the members of the civil rights and against apartheid towards us, we will succeed, because together we are stronger.”
Janet Jackson, The Weeknd, Sean Mendez, Cardi B, Jianll Mona is only part of the star performers who will perform at a festival in New York this year, and will be hosted by Deborah-Li Fernness and Hugh Jackman.
