"According to the government's resolution, the content that was broadcast at 6 a.m. was inappropriate, so they were forced to launch a children's transmission," said Dave Schwartz, Senior Vice-President for Marketing and Public Affairs Bellator, when he was asked about a televised address.
"Peppa Pig," yes."
Bellator President Scott Cocker has vowed to work on a broadcast schedule to reach viewers in the United Kingdom in the future.
