"However, now it's on Sunday, 6 a.m. and we won't be able to do anything while we don't have a Sunday, and they're on Monday.
However, we are working on it.
Verify me, when the broadcast was switched off, we received a lot of messages that we responded to, and the text of these mess was not very friendly.
We thought it was a technical malfunction, and we tried to eliminate it.
However, it turned out that it was an inconsistency with government regulations.
I can promise that this will not happen again.
We'll reduce the tournament to five fights instead of six as usual. We've tried to redirect the signal to the fans, but so far we've delayed these attempts.
A really unfavorable situation.'
